From: Calaos <https://github.com/calaos/calaos_base>
Subject: [PATCH] cpptui: do not invoke a registered key callback through the map node

Local patch carried by Calaos against the vendored copy of jonoton/cpp-tui
(upstream commit 9543ee3c056583eea1fc44491c6c240f0df0b570). Applies on top of
0001-allow-ctrl-c-interception-to-be-disabled.patch.

Why
---
Step "1.7 Registered Key Events" of App::run() invokes the callback through the
unordered_map iterator and then re-reads the same node:

    auto it = key_events_.find(kv);
    if (it != key_events_.end()) {
      it->second.callback();
      if (it->second.consume) {

key_events_ is an unordered_map and unregister_key() erases from it, so a
callback that unregisters its own key destroys the very node it is running
from. Two separate undefined behaviours follow:

  a) the node owns the std::function, so the closure is freed while its
     operator() is still on the stack — anything the lambda touches after the
     unregister call, including its own captures, is a use-after-free;
  b) `it->second.consume` is then read from the freed node.

register_key() from inside a callback is the same hazard by another route: an
insert may rehash the table and invalidate `it` even when nothing is erased.

This is not theoretical. calaos_config's TUI calls updateShortcutState() from
inside its '?', 'i', 'v', 'q' and 's' callbacks (via openDialog()), and that
unregisters exactly those letter shortcuts — the callback erases itself on
every one of those keypresses. It has never crashed observably, which is the
usual luck of freed-but-not-yet-reused memory. Built against the pristine
upstream header, a minimal app whose callback calls unregister_key() on its own
key reports both faults under -fsanitize=address:

    ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free
    READ of size 1 ... in cpptui::App::run(...) cpptui.hpp:16650
    freed by ... cpptui::App::unregister_key(int, bool, bool, bool) cpptui.hpp:16201

What
----
Copy the RegisteredKey out of the map before invoking it, and read consume from
the copy. RegisteredKey is { std::function<void()>; bool; } — copyable, and the
copy keeps the closure alive for the duration of the call no matter what the
callback does to key_events_.

Behaviour is otherwise unchanged: the same callback runs at the same point in
the dispatch order with the same consume semantics. The only cost is one
std::function copy per handled keypress, which is noise at human typing rates.

The copy is taken before the call on purpose. Copying only the callback and
reading consume afterwards would still touch the dead node, and re-doing the
find() after the call would look up an entry the callback may have just
removed or replaced.

Upstream status
---------------
Proposed upstream, see patches/UPSTREAM.md for the submission text. Drop this
patch as soon as the fix is released upstream.

Applying
--------
From the top of the calaos_base tree, after 0001 has been applied:

    patch -p1 < src/lib/cpptui/patches/0002-copy-registered-key-before-invoking-callback.patch
    # or
    git apply src/lib/cpptui/patches/0002-copy-registered-key-before-invoking-callback.patch
---
diff --git a/src/lib/cpptui/cpptui.hpp b/src/lib/cpptui/cpptui.hpp
--- a/src/lib/cpptui/cpptui.hpp
+++ b/src/lib/cpptui/cpptui.hpp
@@ -16651,18 +16651,23 @@ class App {
           }
         }
 
         // 1.7 Registered Key Events
         if (event.is_key_event()) {
           KeyBinding kv = {event.key, event.ctrl, event.alt, event.shift};
           auto it = key_events_.find(kv);
           if (it != key_events_.end()) {
-            it->second.callback();
-            if (it->second.consume) {
+            // The callback may register or unregister keys, including its own,
+            // which erases this node or rehashes the map: that would destroy
+            // the std::function while it runs and leave `it` dangling for the
+            // consume read below. Work on a copy.
+            RegisteredKey binding = it->second;
+            binding.callback();
+            if (binding.consume) {
               needs_render = true;
               continue;  // Consumed, skip subsequent dispatch steps
             }
             needs_render = true;
           }
         }
 
         // 2. Focused Widget Dispatch (Keys only)
